// Measured from the designer's image, 500 by 317 pixels: hoist 12 and fly 19 are
// that image's proportion rounded (derived). Bars 5:2:5 and triangle depth 7 of 12 (derived).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Demiromantic Pride Flag"
  designer "Queer As Cat (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2015-03-08"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20160825145647/http://queerascat.tumblr.com/post/113028340901/demiromantic-and-gray-aromantic-flags-after"
  source "https://crwflags.com/FoTW/FLAGS/qq-arom.html"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Demiromantic_Pride_Flag.svg"
  note "Designer's own Tumblr post, read from the Wayback snapshot above (Tumblr metadata dates it 2015-03-08). The blogger proposes recoloring the demisexual flag's purple to aromantic green for demiromantic, and the post's image is the flag. The post implies that a demiromantic flag with the demisexual purple was already in use, and the blogger writes that they are probably not the first to think of the change; FOTW credits Queer As Cat with this green flag, citing this post. The post gives no hex values, proportion or construction."
  note "Everything numeric was measured from the post's flag image (500 by 317 PNG, fetched from Tumblr's media server). Colors: white #ffffff, green #339933, grey #d2d2d2, black triangle #000000. Bars: 132.5, 52 and 132.5 pixels of 317, which is 5:2:5 to within a pixel. The triangle's apex is 184.5 pixels from the hoist, 0.582 of the height; 7 of 12 is 0.583."
  note "The Commons drawing (MarcoSnail, 2019) copies the demisexual drawing's 5:2:5 bars and 3:5 shape, with a triangle depth of 0.6375 of the height, and uses green #338a37. The designer's image differs from it in green, triangle depth and proportion."
}
palette {
  white "#ffffff"
  green "#339933"
  grey "#d2d2d2"
  black "#000000"
}
proportion hoist=12 fly=19

bars white green grey {
  ratio 5 2 5
}

chevrons black {
  depth 7
}
